# An ALLOWLIST: everything is excluded, then only the code the demo runs is
# let in. So no database, no .env, no key, no tool cache and no dashboard can
# reach the image by accident, whatever is lying around the working folder.
# The same file sits at the repository root, which is what Docker reads by
# default; this copy is what fly.toml names. Keep them identical.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!src/
!src/**
!demo/
!demo/**
!scripts/arc-demo/
!scripts/arc-demo/**
!deploy/fly/entrypoint.sh
**/node_modules
**/.env*
**/*.env
**/*.db
**/*.db.*
**/*.sqlite*
**/*.jsonl
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/secrets/
